anding financial advantage. He has raised roughly ten times what Democrat Raymond Smith Jr. has, and holds over $2.6 million on hand against Smith's $74,000. Most expert raters place the race in the Safe or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Smith only about a 15 percent chance.\n\nSmith, a state legislator with endorsements from groups like VoteVets, has run a visible campaign in a district recently redrawn, and a single August poll showed a surprisingly narrow 3-point race. Still, that poll is dated and partisan-sponsored, and the weight of evidence favors Murphy, though not by a landslide margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1036, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -9.0}]}